==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*2 [[Techn-Old Hyena]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.
*4 [[Doctor K.O.]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Doctor K.O.]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Most threats can be dealt with red attackers like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. For Doctor K.O., you can use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] for massive damage. Techn-Old is the main threat, but can be stalled easily due to their long attack animation. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can rush in and deal large damage to Techn-Old. You should also use [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] to chip peons and Nyandam, as he outranges K.O. and can easily hit Techn-Old with proper timing, dealing massive damage to both. [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)| Rapper cat]] works very well in this stage, thanks to its resistance to red and its Sage Slayer ability.

